WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:01.970
- [Narrator] Tucked away in Budapest,

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:06.770
Vajdahunyad Castle is medieval
in look but not in age.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.103
(airy electronic music)

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.360
Built in 1896, this architectural
complex was designed

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.810
to celebrate the first millennium
of the Hungarian state.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.980
The buildings were
supposed to be temporary,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.830
so they were made of wooden
planks and cardboard designs.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.660
But Hungarians loved them so much,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.673
they were rebuilt with permanent
materials in the 1900s.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.440
The celebratory site
features copies of landmarks

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.350
from all over the larger
19th-Century Hungarian kingdom,

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.353
combining architectural
details of 21 buildings,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.750
like the Romanesque Church of Yak,

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.590
originally located in western Hungary;

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.370
or the Vajdahunyad, or Corvin Castle,

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.140
located in what is now Romania,

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.040
and more commonly known to
fans of the Dracula myth.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.930
It's believed that Vlad the Impaler

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.450
was once imprisoned there.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.170
The name of the Romanian
Castle ended up being adopted

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.670
by Budapestians for the whole compound.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.650
Several Austrian palaces
are represented, as well,

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.690
featuring a blend of Renaissance
and Baroque architecture,

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.480
demonstrating the diversity of styles

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.660
that spread across the
Austria-Hungarian Empire.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.120
And just like the castles
it's built to imitate,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.780
Vajdahunyad is built to be defended.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:22.140
It's accessible only by four bridges,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.090
stretching across the surrounding lake.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.830
For over a century, the castle
has continued to be enjoyed

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.970
by Budapestians and tourists alike

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.973
who come to relish in this
truly Hungarian artifact.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.247
(poppy electronic music)

